{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Azure DevOps.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Azure DevOps.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"azure dev ops azure dev ops","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Azure DevOps.md","fileName":"Azure DevOps.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Azure DevOps","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:52\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Continuous Integration and Delivery]] [[Azure DevOps Work Planning and Traceability]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Continuous Integration and Delivery","Azure DevOps Work Planning and Traceability","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Azure DevOps.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Azure DevOps.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"azure dev ops azure dev ops","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Azure DevOps.md","fileName":"Azure DevOps.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Azure DevOps","heading":"Azure DevOps","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Azure DevOps is the service used in the book to host source code and automate the application's build and release flow. Repository changes trigger a build pipeline, and successful artifacts move through a release pipeline toward Azure staging and production resources.\n\nThe service coordinates the workflow, but the pipeline definition supplies its actual guarantees. Compilation, tests, artifact boundaries, deployment settings, and promotion rules must all be made explicit.\n\nBeyond delivery automation, an Azure DevOps project joins boards and hierarchical work items with repositories, package feeds, test plans, and pipelines so requirements and sprint work can be traced to code and release evidence.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Continuous Integration and Delivery","Azure DevOps Work Pla